Subject: [PATCH 08/10] docs: describe Masakari PowerOps fencing

---
 releasenotes/notes/powerops-ironic-fencing.yaml | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 releasenotes/notes/powerops-ironic-fencing.yaml

diff --git a/releasenotes/notes/powerops-ironic-fencing.yaml b/releasenotes/notes/powerops-ironic-fencing.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3871473
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/powerops-ironic-fencing.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+---
+features:
+  - |
+    Adds an opt-in PowerOps host-recovery integration. PowerOps is disabled by
+    default. When enabled, it requires an etcd-compatible
+    ``[coordination]backend_url`` for tooz coordination and the
+    ``openstacksdk`` dependency to fence failed hosts through Ironic.
+
+    Add ``ironic_fence`` to the configured pre-task list in
+    ``[taskflow_driver_recovery_flows]`` to fence a failed host before its
+    recovery flow continues. While PowerOps is enabled, evacuations are
+    serialized through the shared coordination backend; disabled deployments
+    retain the existing evacuation behavior.
